  "question": {
    "text": "The angle of elevation of the top&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;of a tower from the feet of one person standing due south of the tower is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;and from the feet of another person standing due west of the tower is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></math>. If the height of the tower is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;meters, then the distance (in meters) between the two persons is equal to",
    "image": null
